1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,990
Good evening.

2
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:02,110
How are you?

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:03,810
You look great.

4
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:05,050
Well,

5
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:07,460
you're in the dark, but I can feel that

6
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:08,230
you look great.

7
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:10,120
Let me tell you about something that

8
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:11,170
destroyed my family.

9
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:12,710
Not war.

10
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:14,790
Not an inheritance.

11
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:15,770
No.

12
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:18,390
The family WhatsApp group.

13
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,890
The group is called "United Family".

14
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:24,340
If you need to write "united"

15
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:26,690
in the name, there's already a problem.

16
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,480
Nobody creates a group called

17
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:31,350
"Family That Talks Normally".

18
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:34,310
There are 47 people in the group.

19
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:35,770
47!

20
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:38,450
I know 11 of them.

21
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:41,130
The other 36 are cousins.

22
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,610
I've never met them.

23
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:46,720
But every morning at 6 a.m., they send me

24
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,750
"Good morning" with a spinning rose.

25
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:51,960
A spinning rose, with glitter and

26
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:52,770
music.

27
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:54,770
Six in the morning!

28
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:57,920
I didn't even know glitter

29
00:00:57,920 --> 00:00:59,310
could make noise.

30
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:01,070
And then there's my mom.

31
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:03,490
My mom on WhatsApp

32
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,150
is a 24-hour news channel.

33
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:07,950
She shares everything.

34
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:09,090
Everything!

35
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:10,250
"Urgent:

36
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:11,970
stop eating bananas,

37
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:12,970
it's the government."

38
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:14,750
Mom,

39
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:18,000
who is "the government"? "I don't know,

40
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,150
but it's urgent."

41
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:20,850
And my mom doesn't type.

42
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:23,530
My mom sends voice messages.

43
00:01:23,980 --> 00:01:26,150
Eight-minute voice messages.

44
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:27,470
Eight minutes!

45
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:30,280
For the first seven minutes, she's looking for

46
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:31,130
the button.

47
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:33,800
You hear: "Hello?

48
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:36,110
Hello? Is it recording?"

49
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:37,510
And my dad in the background:

50
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,030
"Press the microphone!"

51
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:40,530
"I AM pressing it!"

52
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:43,980
And at the end, in the last minute, she says:

53
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,890
"Okay, call me back."

54
00:01:46,020 --> 00:01:47,990
Eight minutes to tell me to call her!

55
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:49,370
My dad, though,

56
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:50,330
is different.

57
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:53,350
My dad answers everything with one emoji.

58
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:54,770
The thumbs-up.

59
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,770
Always the thumbs-up.

60
00:01:57,140 --> 00:01:58,510
My sister wrote:

61
00:01:58,880 --> 00:01:59,790
"I'm getting married!"

62
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:00,850
Thumbs-up.

63
00:02:01,340 --> 00:02:02,090
My cousin:

64
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:03,350
"I passed my driving test!"

65
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:04,530
Thumbs-up.

66
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:06,930
My aunt: "The cat died."

67
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,660
Thumbs-up. We don't know if my dad is

68
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:10,110
happy,

69
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:12,560
sad, or if his thumb just

70
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:13,590
got stuck.

71
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:15,740
And the worst is when someone leaves

72
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:16,410
the group.

73
00:02:17,060 --> 00:02:19,220
My cousin Karim left the group

74
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:19,650
once.

75
00:02:20,260 --> 00:02:21,230
Just once.

76
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:23,880
Three minutes later, my aunt

77
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:24,530
added him back.

78
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:26,550
And right below, my mom:

79
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,740
"Why did you leave?

80
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:29,530
Are you upset?

81
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:31,250
Have you eaten?"

82
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:32,650
"Have you eaten?"… seriously!

83
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:33,800
In our family,

84
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:35,310
every crisis gets solved with:

85
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:36,410
"Have you eaten?"

86
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:38,870
Karim never left the group again.

87
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:42,520
Today, Karim sends spinning

88
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,130
roses.

89
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:44,270
They got him.

90
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,910
They turned him.

91
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:46,930
Me,

92
00:02:47,260 --> 00:02:49,120
I tried to put the group on

93
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:49,850
mute.

94
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:51,990
But my mom felt it.

95
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:53,670
She called me:

96
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:55,750
"Did you mute the group?"

97
00:02:56,620 --> 00:02:59,040
Mom, how do you know?

98
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:00,250
"I'm your mother."

99
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,410
No signal,

100
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,470
no wifi, but she knows.

101
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:05,650
Thank you, you're amazing!

102
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:09,020
And join the group, we'll send you

103
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:09,650
a rose!
